plication logs should consist of  all of your process and backing service  logs together so what does that mean  well  if you have an application and it has a  postgres database and a worker process  the logs fed application should have the  you know not only the web server code  but also the worker logs  as well as the database logs combined  into some form that you can search  so this story is the most like damaging  one i'm going to reveal to you today  and trust me there are way bigger things  that i've screwed up but this one is  definitely the worst i feel comfortable  sharing on a stage  uh basically that conference calling  application the way it worked  is we were making money every minute  that people stayed on these free  teleconferencing lines  we would make approximately 50 cents per  minute us which is a lot of money  because we had you know thousands of  users using these conference lines all  the time  so the way everything was architected  was something like this  i had a bunch of asterisk servers that  handle all the phone calls  and i had a web app that people could  use to manage their phone their  teleconferencing lines  and i had an api service i wrote which  was sort of the central source of truth  for everything  so when a call came in this conference  call service would receive an api  request from an astra server and it  would say okay  i'm going to log some billable call  details  and all these logs made their way into a  file called calls.csv  on that server now the reason this is  important is because once a month what i  would have to do  is copy that calls.csv file from the  server onto my laptop  and then i would have to do some like  data manipulation then send it to the  phone company and that's how we would  get paid this is like the way we made  our revenue  um and so one day it's about halfway  through the month  and i decided to copy the calls.csv file  onto my laptop  to do some analysis to see how much  money have we generated